Declare rules_go's generated SDK repo rules reproducible so they can use the repo contents
cache.

Upstream marked `go_download_sdk_rule` reproducible but stopped short of the three repos
derived from it, each of which only writes a generated BUILD/bzl file from its own
attributes: `go_toolchains`, `io_bazel_rules_nogo` and `go_host_compatible_sdk_label`.
Without this they are refetched on every CI runner.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/go/private/extensions.bzl b/go/private/extensions.bzl
index 373d41d..637e9d0 100755
--- a/go/private/extensions.bzl
+++ b/go/private/extensions.bzl
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ def host_compatible_toolchain_impl(ctx):
 HOST_COMPATIBLE_SDK = Label({})
 """.format(repr(ctx.attr.toolchain)))
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks ctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(ctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return ctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 host_compatible_toolchain = repository_rule(
     implementation = host_compatible_toolchain_impl,
     attrs = {
